   "subject": "handling missing data in Multilevel SEM",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Hi, <div><br></div><div>I am currently trying to model Multilevel SEM with lavaan package. I have read online from a Nov 2017 presentation that version 0.6-1 is in development and cannot handle missing data for now. I currently have 0.6-3 version and cannot get it to function yet. May I ask if anyone know of updates, and whether it can handle missing data soon? </div><div><br></div><div>Any help would be much appreciated.</div><div><br></div><div>Best, <br>Cyanea</div></div>\r\n"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "_hrZKbLfAQAJ",
   "from": "Terrence Jorgensen",
   "author": "3fe90052fbf2f899",
   "date": "2018-11-29T10:16:11Z",
   "subject": "Re: handling missing data in Multilevel SEM",
   "parts": [
    [
     2,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><p style=\"margin:0px 0px 1.2em!important\"></p><div><p></p><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div>whether it can handle missing data soon? </div></div></blockquote><p></p></div><p style=\"margin:0px 0px 1.2em!important\"></p>\r\n</div></div>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><p style=\"margin:0px 0px 1.2em!important\">FIML is still not available for MSEM, but you can use multiple imputation (e.g., using the <code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:pre-wrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);background-color:rgb(248,248,248);border-radius:3px;display:inline\">mice</code> package in R, or the Blimp software outside of R).  When you have saved each imputed data set as a <code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:pre-wrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);background-color:rgb(248,248,248);border-radius:3px;display:inline\">list</code> of <code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:pre-wrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);background-color:rgb(248,248,248);border-radius:3px;display:inline\">data.frame</code>s, then you can pass it as the <code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:pre-wrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);background-color:rgb(248,248,248);border-radius:3px;display:inline\">data=</code> argument of <code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:pre-wrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);background-color:rgb(248,248,248);border-radius:3px;display:inline\">runMI()</code> in the semTools package.  Some features for MSEM (e.g., <code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:pre-wrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);background-color:rgb(248,248,248);border-radius:3px;display:inline\">fitted()</code> and <code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:pre-wrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);background-color:rgb(248,248,248);border-radius:3px;display:inline\">resid()</code>, and therefore the SRMR values from <code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:pre-wrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);background-color:rgb(248,248,248);border-radius:3px;display:inline\">fitMeasures()</code>) will only be available in the development version:</p>\r\n<pre style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;font-size:1em;line-height:1.2em;margin:1.2em 0px\"><code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:pre-wrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);background-color:rgb(248,248,248);border-radius:3px;display:inline;white-space:pre;overflow:auto;border-radius:3px;border:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding:0.5em 0.7em;display:block!important;display:block;overflow-x:auto;padding:0.5em;color:rgb(51,51,51);background:rgb(248,248,248)\">devtools::install_github(&quot;simsem/semTools/semTools&quot;)\r\n</code></pre>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px 0px 1.2em!important\">Terrence D. Jorgensen<br>Assistant Professor, Methods and Statistics<br>Research Institute for Child Development and Education, the University of Amsterdam<br><a href=\"http://www.uva.nl/profile/t.d.jorgensen\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://www.uva.nl/profile/t.d.jorgensen&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792424519700000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1RcPTrG6KyNByK9u7zhh7m\">http://www.uva.nl/profile/t.d.jorgensen</a></p>\r\n<div title=\"MDH:PGJsb2NrcXVvdGUgY2xhc3M9ImdtYWlsX3F1b3RlIiBzdHlsZT0ibWFyZ2luOiAwO21hcmdpbi1s\r\nZWZ0OiAwLjhleDtib3JkZXItbGVmdDogMXB4ICNjY2Mgc29saWQ7cGFkZGluZy1sZWZ0OiAxZXg7\r\nIj48ZGl2IGRpcj0ibHRyIj48ZGl2PndoZXRoZXIgaXQgY2FuIGhhbmRsZSBtaXNzaW5nIGRhdGEg\r\nc29vbj8mbmJzcDs8L2Rpd